b. Conducting education about anti-violence values towards women and children;
c. Conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence;
d. Training for PPT members;
e. Conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence.
- 12 - (3) To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence towards women and children, Regional Government is obligated to provide and organize services for victims in the form of:
a. establishing and facilitating the operation of integrated service institutions for victims by involving relevant community elements; b. encouraging community awareness of the importance of protection for victims.

REGIONAL REGULATION OF SOUTH TANGERANG CITY
NUMBER 3 YEAR 2012
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
MAYOR OF SOUTH TANGERANG,

Considering : a. that women and children biologically and philosophically are vulnerable groups and easily become victims of violence, both violence occurring within the household and that committed outside the household;
b. that violence against women and children is a violation of human rights and a crime against human dignity as well as a form of discrimination that must be eliminated;
c. that protection of women and children victims of violence is one aspect of the duties and responsibilities of regional government in providing protection and services to the community;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a, b, and c, it is deemed necessary to establish Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence by Regional Regulation of South Tangerang City;

